CANNABIS THC,PHENYTOIN-FOSPHENYTOIN,Major Severity + Established/Probable Documentation,Delayed,Major,Established,Cannabidiol may increase the serum concentration of Fosphenytoin-Phenytoin. Fosphenytoin-Phenytoin may decrease the serum concentration of Cannabidiol.,Cannabidiol may increase the serum concentration of Fosphenytoin-Phenytoin. Fosphenytoin-Phenytoin may decrease the serum concentration of Cannabidiol. Severity Moderate Reliability Rating Good,Monitor for decreased cannabidiol concentrations and effects and monitor for increased fosphenytoin/phenytoin concentrations and effects if these agents are combined. Dose adjustments may be required.,"In a pharmacokinetic study of 12 healthy volunteers, coadministration of the strong CYP3A4 inducer rifampin (600 mg daily for 10 days) and 4 sprays of the tetrahydrocannabinol and cannabidiol oromucosal spray decreased the maximum concentration (Cmax) and AUC of cannabidiol by 51% and 58%, respectively.1 The oral cannabidiol prescribing information states that because coadministration with strong CYP3A4 inducers (ie, phenytoin) will decrease cannabidiol plasma concentrations, a reduction in cannabidiol efficacy may occur.2 Consider an increase in cannabidiol dosage (based on clinical response and tolerability) when coadministered with a strong CYP3A4 inducer.2

