Phenytoin-mediated induction of CYP3A4 likely contributes to reduced cannabidiol concentrations. Cannabidiol-mediated inhibition of CYP2C19 will likely increase phenytoin concentrations and effects.","1. Stott C, White L, Wright S, Wilbraham D, Guy G. A phase I, open-label, randomized, crossover study in three parallel groups to evaluate the effect of rifampicin, ketoconazole, and omeprazole on the pharmacokinetics of THC/CBD oromucosal spray in healthy volunteers. Springerplus. 2013;2(1):236. [PubMed 23750331]

